  "finalText": "I built the kinetic typography piece on a dark background (#0E0E0E), 1080×1080, and extended the composition from 8 s to 10 s so each phrase has time to be read.\n\n- **Phrase 1 – \"Design is not just\"** (off-white, 88 px): words slide up one by one, hold, then lift out.\n- **Phrase 2 – \"what it looks like.\"** (grey, 88 px): same word slide, lifts out before phrase 3 arrives.\n- **Phrase 3 – \"Design is\"** (off-white, 88 px): same treatment, then lifts out.\n- **Phrase 4 – \"how it works.\"** (red #FF4A2E, 128 px): the hero. Words spring in from below with a slight scale overshoot and stay on screen to the end.\n- **Attribution – \"— Steve Jobs\"** (grey, 26 px): fades and rises in at about 8 s, below the hero.\n\nEach phrase leaves upward as the next one enters, so they hand over rather than stacking. The layers are named by phrase.\n\nThe last critique pass scored 73/100. The remaining notes are about adding supporting elements and varying the phrase motion. I left those alone because the piece is meant to stay minimal. I can add a thin red rule under the hero or vary the entrances per phrase if you want more."
